1. Case Overview
Patient: 45-year-old Female  
Suspected Drug: Amoxicillin (Started 5 days prior)  
Adverse Event: Generalized rash, severe itching, nausea, and dizziness  

2. WHO-UMC Causality Assessment System
Classification:PROBABLE / LIKELY
Rationale:
  1. Reasonable Timeframe: The cutaneous reaction occurred 5 days after starting Amoxicillin, which fits the standard onset window for antibiotic hypersensitivity.
  2. Low Confounding Risk:Paracetamol taken p.r.n. is unlikely to cause this clinical presentation.
  3. Re-challenge Status: Re-challenge was not performed due to safety/ethical concerns regarding severe penicillin hypersensitivity. Per WHO criteria, absence of re-challenge places this in the Probable category rather than Certain.

